        "body": "The vulnerability was in the `ping_host` function which used `os.popen(command)` to execute a shell command constructed with user input. This is vulnerable to CWE-78 (OS Command Injection) because the host parameter could contain shell metacharacters that get interpreted by the shell.\n\nThe fix replaces `os.popen()` with `subprocess.run()` and passes the command as a list of arguments instead of a single shell string. This prevents shell interpretation of the input, eliminating the command injection risk. The command is now structured as `[\"ping\", \"-c\", \"1\", host]`, where each argument is passed separately to the ping process, making it safe from shell injection attacks.\n\nThe `subprocess.run()` call also uses `capture_output=True` and `text=True` to maintain the same behavior of returning stdout as a string, while properly handling the command execution without shell interpretation.",
        "changed_files": 1,
        "closed_at": "2026-08-14T16:26:48Z",
